    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires improvements in efficiency of administrative services, quality of service rendered to users, and facilitation of access to information for agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must integrate existing practices of agents, provide intelligent assistance tools, and accompany administrative activities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's PM methodologies, past public sector references, consortium partners, available capacity, and governance practices as of 2024, how can our company's consolidate all agent contributions into a coherent tender response that addresses the client's needs while maintaining decision traceability?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the client's requirements for improving efficiency, quality of service, and access to information, our company's can leverage our company's experience in public sector projects, such as the digital workplace transformation for Comune di Torino and the AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia. our company's will utilize our company's project management methodologies, including PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe, to ensure a structured approach." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's available capacity of 60% as of 2024, our company's can allocate sufficient resources to this project. our company's past experience in leading consortia, with up to 5 partners, will be valuable in integrating the contributions of various agents into a coherent tender response. our company's have worked with known partners like EuroCloud Solutions S.A., LexIA GmbH, and GreenCompute S.r.l., which can provide expertise in areas such as sovereign cloud hosting, legal AI, and green IT." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To maintain decision traceability, our company's will implement our company's typical delivery structure, including governance tools like RAID logs, decision logs, change request processes, and steering committees. our company's reporting cadence of weekly status reports, monthly steering committee meetings, and quarterly executive reviews will ensure that all stakeholders are informed and aligned throughout the project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By consolidating agent contributions through a collaborative approach, facilitated by our company's project management capabilities and supported by our company's consortium experience, our company's can submit a tender response that addresses the client's needs for efficiency, quality of service, and access to information. our company's solution will integrate existing practices, provide intelligent assistance tools, and accompany administrative activities, all while ensuring decision traceability and maintaining our company's low-to-medium risk appetite." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client demands response times below 2 seconds, high availability (99.9%), API integration with existing information systems and user directories, hosting on sovereign infrastructure certified to the level required by the tender within the EU, and no dependency on non-European suppliers. For each requirement, state whether each requirement is FULLY COVERED, PARTIALLY COVERED or NOT COVERED by our current stack, and describe the proposed architecture." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on The client requirements, here are the coverage assessments for each requirement: 1. Response times below 2 seconds: PARTIALLY COVERED our typical performance benchmarks show a p95 response time of 1800 ms, which exceeds the required 2-second threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, our can optimize our architecture to achieve better performance. our propose using our existing LLM models with quantization methods like INT8 or INT4 (GPTQ) to reduce latency. 2. High availability (99.9%): FULLY COVERED our past projects have achieved an average availability of 99.92%, which meets the client's requirement. our can ensure high availability by deploying our solution on a cloud provider with a strong track record, such as OVHcloud or Scaleway, and using containerization with Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) for efficient resource management and monitoring with Prometheus and Grafana. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "API integration with existing information systems and user directories: FULLY COVERED our have extensive experience with API integration, supporting standards like REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, as well as API gateways like Kong and Apigee. our can also integrate with various identity providers, including Active Directory/LDAP, Keycloak, and FranceConnect. 4. Hosting on sovereign infrastructure certified to the level required by the tender within the EU: FULLY COVERED our have experience deploying solutions on SecNumCloud-type infrastructures, such as Outscale (SecNumCloud), which meets the sovereignty requirements. our can ensure that our solution is hosted on infrastructure certified to the level required by the tender within the EU. 5." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "No dependency on non-European suppliers: PARTIALLY COVERED While our can deploy our solution on European cloud providers and use open-source technologies, our cannot guarantee that all our dependencies are free from non-European suppliers. However, our can minimize this risk by carefully selecting our technology stack and ensuring that our primary dependencies are from European or open-source suppliers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The proposed architecture would involve deploying our solution on a sovereign cloud infrastructure within the EU, using containerization and orchestration with Docker and Kubernetes (K8s). our would integrate our solution with the client's existing information systems and user directories using APIs and API gateways. To ensure high availability, our would monitor our solution with Prometheus and Grafana, and optimize performance using quantization methods and efficient resource management." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (EU-only data hosting, no transfer outside EU, encryption and pseudonymisation of sensitive data where applicable), explicability and transparency of recommendations, and a posteriori understanding of elements leading to answers or suggestions. No decision may be automated without explicit validation by an authorised professional." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What security risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the required regulatory frameworks (GDPR, EU AI Act, RGS, SecNumCloud, NIS2) as of 2024? Based on we company context, we can identify some potential security risks related to GDPR compliance, such as the risk of non-compliance with data residency and transfer requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, we standard data residency policy is EU-only, which aligns with the requirement. we also have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside EU unless there is an explicit legal basis. Regarding explicability and transparency, we can provide some level of insight into we AI decision-making processes through tools like Microsoft Presidio for anonymization and custom NER models. we Data Protection Officer (DPO) can be contacted at dpo@nexus-engineering.it for any GDPR-related queries or concerns." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for regulatory compliance, as of 2024, we have experience with RGPD/GDPR, EU AI Act, RGS v2 (ANSSI), SecNumCloud, and NIS2 Directive. we are also ISO 27001 certified, which demonstrates we commitment to information security management. Additionally, we have a Data Protection Officer appointed and are experienced in conducting Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, we must flag the risk of potential non-compliance with certain requirements, such as ensuring that all decisions are validated by an authorized professional. While we do have measures like confidence threshold escalation and model update security review, the explicit validation requirement may necessitate additional controls or processes to be implemented." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of explicability and transparency, we AI security controls include output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and model isolation. Nevertheless, providing a posteriori understanding of elements leading to answers or suggestions might require further enhancements to we existing capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, we are generally compliant with the required regulatory frameworks but must carefully evaluate and address specific requirements and potential risks to ensure full compliance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects compliance with regulatory requirements in force, including GDPR, and adherence to specific standards and contractual clauses. The solution must be designed as a tool of assistance, with no automated decisions without explicit agent validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the necessary legal frameworks and certifications? Based on we company context, we have experience with public procurement in several EU jurisdictions, including Italy, France, Germany, Belgium, and EU institutions. we are also familiar with various procedure types, such as open, restricted, and competitive dialogue procedures." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding GDPR compliance, we standard legal basis is Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest. we have a DPA template version 3.2 and provide support for Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs). However, we note that we operations are intra-EU only, which means no Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) or adequacy decisions are required. we flag the following legal risks: open-source license compliance, cross-border data flow (although cross-border data flow is not an issue for we since we operate within EU), AI Act compliance evolution, and vendor lock-in mitigation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To mitigate these risks, we have a no-copyleft GPL contamination policy, and we use standard licenses such as Apache 2.0, MIT, and LGPL v2.1. we default IP model is work-for-hire, where all deliverables are transferred to the client upon final payment. we also have source code escrow capability through Logitas (France). As for certifications, our company context does not explicitly mention specific certifications." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, we have professional indemnity insurance of 5 million euros and cyber liability insurance of 2 million euros through AXA XL, with a policy valid until December 31, 2025. we are compliant with AI Act, as we have expertise in this area and are aware of prohibited AI practices. we also ensure human oversight contractual enforcement and have a no-automated decision without human validation policy. In terms of contractual clauses, we have a standard SLA penalty mechanism, termination for cause notice days (30 days), and termination for convenience notice days (90 days). we also provide data return on termination within 30 days and offer a data destruction certificate. we price revision mechanism is based on annual indexation capped at the official national index, with a maximum of 3% per year." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, while we have measures in place to address various legal risks and comply with necessary frameworks, it is essential to carefully review the client's specific requirements and ensure that we capabilities align with the client's expectations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client's global budget is 3 million euros over 4 years, with annual operating costs to remain controlled and compatible with The client's budgetary capacity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires a pilot phase followed by progressive rollout." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimisation strategies our can propose while ensuring quality of service?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our company context, The client's global budget averages to 750,000 euros per year. our pricing model targets a gross margin of 28%, but our have a minimum acceptable margin of 18%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To determine our projected margin on this contract, our would need to estimate the costs associated with delivering the service." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, given that our standard daily rates range from 550 to 1050 euros and our infrastructure margin is 12%, our can propose a cost structure that meets The client's global budget while ensuring our minimum acceptable margin." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Considering our current financial position, with an annual revenue of 4.2 million euros and a net profit of 380,000 euros, taking on a contract of this size would be manageable. our debt-to-equity ratio is 0.42, indicating a relatively healthy financial situation, and our current cash position of 520,000 euros provides a cushion for initial investments." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for cost-optimisation strategies, our could propose the following:  1) Renegotiate rates with subcontractors to reduce variable costs, which account for 65% of project costs. 2) Implement scope reduction by removing optional modules or reducing training days if necessary, while maintaining the core service quality. 3) Ensure efficient project management to minimize overhead costs, which are currently at 145,000 euros per month." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By carefully managing these factors and leveraging our existing capabilities, our can aim to achieve our target gross margin of 28% on this contract while ensuring the quality of service expected by the client." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client seeks an artificial intelligence solution that assists agents in agents daily missions, providing intelligent assistance tools, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can our LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, and performance benchmarks support the development of such a solution, and what innovation strategies can our propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk58> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l., can support the development of an artificial intelligence solution that assists agents in agents daily missions by leveraging our LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, and performance benchmarks.  our have experience with several large language models, including Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3 8B, CamemBERT, and Falcon 7B, which can be used to provide intelligent assistance tools. our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, is an EU-origin model with a strong French-language performance, making Our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct suitable for this task. our LLM stack, RAG capabilities can facilitate access to information by providing retrieval strategies such as dense vector semantic search, BM25 sparse search, and hybrid search. our also have experience with various vector stores, including Qdrant, Weaviate, pgvector, and FAISS, which can be used to store and retrieve relevant information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk59> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To improve answer quality, our can use our fine-tuning methods, such as LoRA, QLoRA, and full fine-tune on domain corpus. our average accuracy gain from fine-tuning is around 12%, which can significantly enhance the performance of the solution. our explainability tools, including source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME, can provide transparency into the decision-making process of the model. provide is particularly important in a public administration setting where accountability and trust are crucial." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk60> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of innovation strategies, our can propose several approaches." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk61> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "First, we can leverage our current research topics, such as knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and multi-agent collaboration frameworks, to develop a solution that integrates with existing practices and systems." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk62> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Second, our can utilize our experience with open-source contributions, including LangChain plugins, RAG evaluation toolkit, and French NER model, to develop a customized solution that meets the client's specific needs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Finally, our can prioritize the development of a solution that is compliant with regulatory requirements, such as the EU AI Act, and ensures data sovereignty by hosting data exclusively on European Union territory." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk64> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This aligns with our values and expertise in developing solutions that meet strict regulatory standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk65> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, our has the necessary capabilities, expertise, and innovation strategies to support the development of an artificial intelligence solution that assists agents in agents daily missions and meets the client's requirements and constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk66> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client aims to reduce The client environmental footprint, proposing a solution that contributes to the reduction of energetic consumption and relies on infrastructures with low carbon impact. Our company has an EcoVadis rating, a known carbon footprint, green hosting partners, digital sobriety practices, social commitments, AI ethics principles, and known sustainability trade-offs as of 2024." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk67> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "How can Our company ensure Our company solution aligns with the client's environmental goals and CSR expectations? To ensure our solution aligns with the client's environmental goals and CSR expectations, Our company can highlight Our company existing sustainability efforts and capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk68> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company have an EcoVadis rating of Silver with a score of 62, indicating Our company commitment to corporate social responsibility. Our company carbon footprint is known, with total Scope 1 and 2 emissions of 148 tCO2e as of the last bilan carbone conducted in 2023, and Our company aim to reach net zero by 2040." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk69> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of reducing energetic consumption, Our company partner with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, both based in France and using 100% renewable energy, which helps minimize Our company carbon footprint. Our company digital sobriety practices, such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy, contribute to reducing energy consumption by an estimated 35% compared to baseline operations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk70> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company also prioritize social commitments, including a strong gender equality index of 88, disabled workers making up 4.2% of Our company workforce, and a preference for local subcontracting. Our company AI ethics principles ensure transparency, fairness, and human oversight in all AI-driven processes, which can support the client's goals by providing ethical and responsible solutions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk71> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Moreover, Our company are aware of common sustainability trade-offs, such as balancing high availability with energy consumption, and Our company have standard resolutions in place to address common sustainability trade-offs, such as balancing high availability with energy consumption, like using low-power standby modes or recommending renewable energy certificates. By leveraging these capabilities and commitments, our solution can contribute to reducing the client's environmental footprint while meeting the client's CSR expectations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. partners, including EuroCloud Solutions S.A., LexIA GmbH, and GreenCompute S.r.l., is pleased to submit a proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in municipal agents daily missions for the City of Belval. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has extensive experience in public sector projects, such as the digital workplace transformation for Comune di Torino and the AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval will provide intelligent assistance tools to facilitate access to information, improve the quality of answers, and reduce processing times. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will utilize Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Large Language Model (LLM) stack, including models such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3 8B, CamemBERT, and Falcon 7B, which can be fine-tuned to provide accurate and relevant responses. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities will enable efficient access to information through dense vector semantic search, BM25 sparse search, and hybrid search." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure high availability, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will deploy an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval on a sovereign cloud infrastructure within the European Union, such as Outscale (SecNumCloud), which meets the required level of certification. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will also implement containerization with Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) for efficient resource management and monitoring with Prometheus and Grafana. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval will guarantee a high level of availability, with an objective of 99.9%, and response times below 2 seconds. In terms of security and compliance, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will ensure that an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval respects the regulatory requirements in force, including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will host data exclusively on the European Union territory, with no transfers outside the European Union, and protect sensitive data through encryption and anonymization. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. Data Protection Officer (DPO) will be available to address any the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)-related queries or concerns. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval will also provide explicability and transparency into the decision-making process of the model, using tools such as source citation, chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, and LIME." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk76> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will ensure that all decisions are validated by an authorized professional, with no automated decisions without explicit validation. In terms of integration, an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval will be designed to integrate with the existing information systems and user directories of the City of Belval, using APIs and API gateways such as Kong and Apigee. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will also ensure that an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval is compatible with the existing practices of the agents and does not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk77> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. pricing model targets a gross margin of 28%, but Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a minimum acceptable margin of 18%. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. estimate that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. costs associated with delivering the service will be manageable within the client's global budget of 3 million euros over 4 years. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. propose a cost structure that meets the client's budget while ensuring Nexus Engineering S.r.l. minimum acceptable margin, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. are open to discussing cost-optimization strategies, such as renegotiating rates with subcontractors or implementing scope reduction." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk78> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is committed to sustainability and corporate social responsibility (CSR). Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have an EcoVadis rating of Silver, with a score of 62, and aim to reach net zero by 2040. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. partner with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, which use 100% renewable energy, and implement digital sobriety practices such as model quantization, auto-scaling, and query result caching to reduce energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk79> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In conclusion, an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval meets the requirements of the City of Belval for an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in municipal agents daily missions. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. are confident that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. expertise, experience, and commitment to sustainability and CSR make Nexus Engineering S.r.l. an ideal partner for this project. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. look forward to the opportunity to discuss an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval in further detail and explore how we can work together to deliver a successful outcome." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

